From: xiaobao <xiaobao@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 09:50:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: dwc: extend link-up wait window to ~10s for
 slow-training endpoints

On ROCEOS K50S MAX (RK3568), the lane1 RTL8125 of the bifurcated
PCIe3.0 x2 (pcie3x1, fe270000) finishes link training later than the
default ~1s dw_pcie_wait_for_link() window (10 retries x ~95ms), so
every boot logs "Phy link never came up" and the third 2.5G NIC is
missing -- yet the endpoint is perfectly healthy: a manual
"echo 1 > /sys/bus/pci/rescan" later finds 0001:11:00.0 and r8169
binds it. Pure boot-time wait-window problem.

Bump LINK_WAIT_MAX_RETRIES 10 -> 100 (~10s worst case). The loop
breaks as soon as the link is up, so boards with fast links are
unaffected; the only cost is up to ~9s extra boot time on a slot
where no device is ever present (not the case on K50S MAX: all
three PCIe slots are populated).

Signed-off-by: xiaobao <xiaobao@local>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.h
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.h
@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@
 	set_bit(DW_PCIE_CAP_ ## _cap, &(_pci)->caps)
 
 /* Parameters for the waiting for link up routine */
-#define LINK_WAIT_MAX_RETRIES		10
+#define LINK_WAIT_MAX_RETRIES		100
 #define LINK_WAIT_USLEEP_MIN		90000
 #define LINK_WAIT_USLEEP_MAX		100000
 
